WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.540
Look at a normal embryo and you cannot tell whether a tissue's fate is fixed or

2
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.960
instructed by its neighbours.

3
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.260
You cannot tell what a region sends, or what it can receive.

4
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.540
So move the tissue.

5
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:23.300
Put it in a new place, a new time or a new host, and read what it does.

6
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:27.263
Pick a donor region and a host embryo.

7
00:00:28.303 --> 00:00:31.783
Donor and host can be the same stage, or different ages.

8
00:00:32.723 --> 00:00:36.203
The piece can go back to its own place, or to a new one.

9
00:00:37.263 --> 00:00:44.223
Spemann devised thin glass needles and wax plates with tiny wells to hold the egg still.

10
00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:47.413
Donor and host must be told apart.

11
00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:53.813
A graft looks like its host, so a second axis might simply be the graft growing

12
00:00:53.813 --> 00:00:55.213
according to its origin.

13
00:00:56.193 --> 00:01:00.593
Spemann and Mangold used newt species that differed in pigmentation.

14
00:01:01.553 --> 00:01:04.273
For birds, Le Douarin's marker is natural.

15
00:01:05.193 --> 00:01:10.353
Quail nuclei carry a large block of condensed chromatin that chick nuclei lack.

16
00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:13.473
The mark does not fade as cells divide.

17
00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:18.007
Let the host develop, then fix and section it.

18
00:01:18.887 --> 00:01:22.687
Pigmented cells in the new structure are host cells that were induced.

19
00:01:23.607 --> 00:01:25.087
Pale cells are donor cells.

20
00:01:26.007 --> 00:01:31.387
For birds, graft a short piece of quail neural tube into a chick embryo at the same

21
00:01:31.387 --> 00:01:37.527
axial level. Quail cells that emigrate can be recognised in sections long afterwards.

22
00:01:37.917 --> 00:01:41.537
A structure made of host cells shows instruction.

23
00:01:42.237 --> 00:01:46.097
A structure made of donor cells shows self-differentiation.

24
00:01:46.797 --> 00:01:48.117
The marker decides which.

25
00:01:49.117 --> 00:01:55.717
In this idealised example, 120 of 1,200 neural tube cells are unpigmented.

26
00:01:56.137 --> 00:02:01.377
That is about 10% donor, so about 90% host cells were induced.

27
00:02:02.317 --> 00:02:08.877
Of 310 notochord cells, 300 are unpigmented: about 97% donor.

28
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:14.330
Our graft is also a wound, so wound effects need a control.

29
00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:20.670
A natural pigment is not shared evenly by every descendant, so an injected dye can

30
00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:24.530
be used instead. Grafting itself may make artefacts.

31
00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:30.210
In Xenopus neural crest mapping, the team repeated the result with three methods.

32
00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:37.490
One injected a fluorescent dextran into a single blastomere, to label crest without grafting.

33
00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:45.310
In 1924, Spemann and Mangold reported grafting a small piece of dorsal lip from a

34
00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:48.210
pale newt gastrula into a pigmented one.

35
00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:53.830
A second body axis formed, and most of its neural tube was host tissue.

36
00:02:55.010 --> 00:03:00.650
From the early 1970s, Le Douarin and colleagues made quail chick chimeras.

37
00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:06.710
The permanent nuclear mark followed cells that left the graft, and mapped which

38
00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:11.910
level of the neural tube gives, for example, the face skeleton, ganglia, adrenal

39
00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.330
medulla and gut neurons.

40
00:03:14.283 --> 00:03:21.083
In 1976, Hollyday and Hamburger grafted an extra leg onto chick embryos.

41
00:03:21.923 --> 00:03:28.223
More motor neurons survived, but day six counts, before the normal loss, showed no

42
00:03:28.223 --> 00:03:37.003
extra. In cases selected for vigorous motility, the gain was 11.0% to 27.5%.

43
00:03:37.003 --> 00:03:41.063
The graft changed target size without touching the cord.

44
00:03:41.063 --> 00:03:47.963
A graft shows what a tissue does in a new place, and the marker says whose cells did it.
